cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Chemistry-resolved disagreement between PBE and r2SCAN stability verdicts in the
  GNoME materials database — analysis code and derived results
message: >-
  If you use this software or its derived results, please cite both the software (this
  file) and the preprint it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Karthikeya
    affiliation: Accretion Labs
    email: founder@accretionlabs.net
repository-code: https://github.com/FOUNDERACCRETION/gnome-audit
license: MIT
keywords:
  - density functional theory
  - r2SCAN
  - meta-GGA
  - thermodynamic stability
  - convex hull
  - materials discovery
  - GNoME
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, pre-registered decision rules and derived results for a chemistry-resolved
  audit of disagreement between PBE(+U) and r2SCAN stability verdicts on the 139,541 GNoME
  materials released with r2SCAN recalculations. Includes cluster-bootstrap and
  cluster-robust uncertainty over structural-prototype clusters, a propensity model for
  recomputation selection, and a held-out verification-budget evaluation. Reproduces from
  two public CSV files; two phases additionally require a free Materials Project API key.
